update articles set body = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>Velana International Airport, widely known as <a href="/maldives/islands/male/">Male</a> Airport, is the main international gateway to the breathtaking islands of the Maldives. Situated on Hulhule Island, a short distance from the capital city, Male, this airport is a crucial hub for travelers from around the globe. Offering state-of-the-art facilities, extensive connectivity, and world-class services, Male Airport plays a vital role in the Maldivian tourism industry, handling millions of passengers annually.</p><p>The Maldives is renowned for its idyllic beaches, crystal-clear waters, and luxurious resorts. Whether you''re arriving for a family vacation, a romantic getaway, or an adventurous solo trip, your journey begins at Velana International Airport. This guide provides an in-depth look at everything you need to know about Male Airport, including its history, facilities, transportation options, and travel tips.</p><h2>Airport Overview</h2><p>Velana International Airport (IATA: MLE, ICAO: VRMM) is the busiest and most prominent airport in the Maldives, serving as the primary entry point for both international tourists and domestic travelers. The airport''s strategic location on Hulhule Island, adjacent to the capital city of Male, makes it an essential hub for air travel in the region.</p><p>Originally known as Hulhule Airport, it was inaugurated in 1960 and has since undergone several expansions and upgrades to accommodate the growing number of visitors to the Maldives. In 2017, the airport was renamed Velana International Airport in honor of Ibrahim Nasir, the second President of the Maldives, who played a significant role in the nation''s development. Today, Velana International Airport is equipped with modern facilities, including a new runway capable of handling the world''s largest aircraft, such as the Airbus A380.</p><h2>Flight Information</h2><p>The Maldives does not currently have direct flights from many countries, so most international visitors connect through a major regional hub — Dubai, Doha, Colombo, Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, and several Indian and European cities all operate direct flights into Velana International Airport. Flight time to Male depends entirely on your origin: it''s around 4-5 hours from the Middle East, 4-6 hours from most of South and Southeast Asia, and 9-11 hours from Europe on a direct service.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/how-to-get-to-maldives.webp" alt="How to get to Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/how-long-is-the-flight-to-maldives.webp" alt="How long is the flight to Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/flights-to-male-maldives.webp" alt="Flights to Male Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h2>Arriving and Departing: Inside the International Terminal</h2><h3>Arrival</h3><p>After getting off your flight, it''s a short walk to the arrival hall (occasionally with a bus transfer on the apron first). From there you''ll go through the immigration counters — queues can be longer on Sundays, the airport''s busiest day. Past immigration, you''ll reach the baggage claim: only 3 baggage rollers serve the whole terminal, so expect a short wait. A baggage control desk sits beside the rollers for reporting any missing or damaged luggage. Next come the security scanners for your hand luggage — note that the Maldives is a 100% Muslim country, so alcohol cannot be carried beyond this point. After the scanners, you''ll reach the exit gate, where resort and hotel staff wait to meet arriving guests, alongside several hotel/resort transfer counters.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-arrival-terminal.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport arrival terminal" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>Departure</h3><p>The departure gates sit to the left of the arrival gate — 4 numbered gates in total. Your passport is checked at the entrance, after which you''ll go through security screening and a baggage scan. Directly ahead of the scanners is the airline check-in counter. Once you''ve passed through, you can''t re-enter the arrival side, so make sure you''re carrying everything you need before proceeding. After check-in, take the escalator or lift up to the first floor to reach your boarding gate — this upper floor also has duty-free shops, a bank, a food court, and a designated smoking area.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-departure-terminal.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport departure terminal" loading="lazy" /></figure><h2>Airport Facilities and Services</h2><p>Velana International Airport is well equipped for travelers passing through, whether for a few hours or overnight.</p><h4>SIM Cards</h4><p>The Maldives currently has 2 mobile operators, Dhiraagu and Ooredoo, both with a service desk at the airport — look for the signboard to the right of the exit.</p><h4>ATM &amp; Bank</h4><p>A Bank of Maldives branch and ATMs are on site, accepting international cards (Visa, Mastercard, Amex). Dedicated USD withdrawal booths are available, and the bank also offers currency exchange.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-atm.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport ATM" loading="lazy" /></figure><h4>Layover Hotel</h4><p>Travelers arriving late at night who need to wait until the next day for a domestic connection can stay at a hotel on airport grounds, a 5-minute free shuttle ride away — the pickup point is on the right of the arrival exit, along the walkway to the domestic terminal.</p><h4>Lounge Service</h4><p>A VIP lounge and a wellness/massage lounge are both available for travelers wanting to shower or relax after a long flight.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-lounge.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport lounge service" loading="lazy" /></figure><h4>Food Court</h4><p>A food court with several international brands sits near the main exit area, close to the departure gate.</p><h4>Information Desk</h4><p>Located at the main gate, for general traveler inquiries and on-the-spot hotel or transfer bookings.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-information-desk.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport information desk" loading="lazy" /></figure><h4>Tourist Police</h4><p>A desk is located next to the wellness lounge in the main waiting hall for reporting missing luggage or other issues. Tourist Police contact number: 332-2111, extension 3322112.</p><h4>Clinic and Pharmacy</h4><p>A health-care center with basic first aid, staffed and operated by Aasandha, is in the terminal building. The airport pharmacy, also run by Aasandha, sits next to the Bank of Maldives ATM and stocks most common medications during flight hours; a second pharmacy is near the main exit.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-pharmacy.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport pharmacy" loading="lazy" /></figure><h4>Post Office</h4><p>A branch of Maldives Post operates inside the airport.</p><h4>Luggage Storage</h4><p>Planning to visit Male city during a long layover? Store your bags at the luggage store near the departure gate for USD 6 per normal-sized bag.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-luggage-store.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport luggage storage" loading="lazy" /></figure><h4>Prayer Room</h4><p>A mosque is available in the waiting hall area, next to the restrooms.</p><h4>Smoking Area</h4><p>Designated smoking areas are provided at the main exit and in both the international and domestic terminal areas. Smoking elsewhere is prohibited and carries a USD 35 fine.</p><h2>Domestic Terminal and Domestic Flights</h2><p>Velana International Airport combines domestic and international flights under one roof. The domestic terminal is about a 3-minute walk from the international arrival gate, on the right-hand side. Check-in counters are right at the entrance, and the boarding gate (with its own hand-luggage scanners) sits directly opposite. There are 16 domestic airports across the Maldives; the furthest, Gan International Airport in the deep south, is about 1 hour 25 minutes away by air. As with the international side, the domestic arrival hall shares baggage rollers with departures in the same building. Domestic flights get busy and are limited in number, so book ahead whenever possible.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/velaana-airport-domestic-terminal.webp" alt="Velana International Airport domestic terminal" loading="lazy" /></figure><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-domestic-transfer-routes.webp" alt="Maldives domestic transfer routes" loading="lazy" /></figure><h2>Getting From the Airport to Your Resort or Island</h2><p>How you continue your journey from Velana International Airport depends entirely on where you''re staying — see our full <a href="/maldives/airport-transfers/">airport transfer guide</a> for options and booking.</p><ul><li><strong>Taxi</strong> — available for guests staying in Male or Hulhumale city only; resort guests need a different transfer method.</li><li><strong>Speedboat</strong> — for resorts and islands in or close to Male Atoll; further-flung islands need a domestic flight or seaplane instead. See our <a href="/maldives/speedboat-transfers/">speedboat transfer</a> options.</li><li><strong>Seaplane</strong> — Velana operates the largest seaplane platform in the world, and it''s one of the most convenient options for distant resorts, since it can take off from the airport and land directly at many properties. Guests on a domestic flight instead will still need a connecting speedboat from the domestic airport to their resort. Seaplane check-in counters are in front of the international arrival gate; after checking in your baggage, the airline provides a short bus transfer to the seaplane terminal.</li></ul><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-information-desk-location.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport information desk location" loading="lazy" /></figure><h2>Airport Free Wi-Fi</h2><p>Velana International Airport offers free Wi-Fi for all travelers. Switch on Wi-Fi on your device, select the airport network, and you''ll be prompted to log in using your Facebook or Gmail account — enter your details and you''ll be connected for up to 1 hour.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/wifi.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport free Wi-Fi" loading="lazy" /></figure><h2>Special Assistance for Passengers</h2><p>If you need a wheelchair or other special assistance, terminal services staff will accompany you from the moment you enter the airport through check-in and boarding. For an unaccompanied minor (age 6-12) or a child travelling alone, simply notify your airline in advance — customer service staff will escort them through the whole check-in process and up to departure.</p><p>For check-in and boarding, staff assisting with special needs will check you in as soon as you arrive at the counter, without requiring you to queue, and will prioritize you during boarding as well.</p><h2>Things to Do During a Layover</h2><p>Long wait between flights or boats? Male island is just 10 minutes from the airport, and two kinds of activities make the most of that time: a guided <a href="/maldives/male-city-tour/">Male City Tour</a> (on foot, by bike, car, or bus, with airport pickup and drop-off) or a day visit to a nearby resort. Either turns dead layover time into a genuine look at the Maldives beyond the airport.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/articles/maldives-international-airport-jetty.webp" alt="Maldives International Airport jetty" loading="lazy" /></figure><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h4>What is Velana International Airport also known as?</h4><p>Velana International Airport (IATA: MLE) is also commonly called Male Airport or Male International Airport, since it sits on Hulhule Island right next to the capital, Male.</p><h4>How do I get from the airport to my resort?</h4><p>By speedboat (Male Atoll resorts), seaplane (more distant resorts), domestic flight plus a connecting speedboat (the furthest atolls), or taxi if you''re staying in Male or Hulhumale city itself.</p><h4>Is there free Wi-Fi at Velana International Airport?</h4><p>Yes — connect to the airport Wi-Fi network and log in with a Facebook or Gmail account for up to 1 hour of free access.</p><h4>Can I store my luggage at the airport?</h4><p>Yes, luggage storage is available near the departure gate for USD 6 per normal-sized bag — useful if you want to visit Male city during a long layover.</p><h4>Is alcohol allowed at the airport?</h4><p>No. The Maldives is a 100% Muslim country, and alcohol cannot be carried past the arrival terminal''s security scanners.</p>' where id = (select id from nodes where node_type='article' and slug='male-airport-velana-international-airport');
update nodes set meta_description = 'Velana International Airport (Male Airport) guide: arrival and departure terminals, airport services, domestic terminal, transfers to your resort, free Wi-Fi, and things to do during a layover.', summary = 'Velana International Airport (Male Airport) guide: arrival and departure terminals, airport services, domestic terminal, transfers to your resort, free Wi-Fi, and things to do during a layover.', updated_at = now() where node_type='article' and slug='male-airport-velana-international-airport';


